-- ═══ 325 KTH Scholarship ═══
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'KTH Scholarship', provider = 'KTH Royal Institute of Technology', coverage_type = 'Full Tuition Waiver', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'Two steps in Sweden''s first (international) admission round: (1) apply for a KTH master''s programme as your FIRST priority at universityadmissions.se by 15 January 2027 and pay the application fee (supporting documents by 1 February 2027); (2) submit the KTH Scholarship application form on the KTH Scholarship page during its application window in the same round - no additional documents are required for the scholarship itself.', deadline_date = '2027-01-15', deadline_type = 'fixed', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Master's"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["Master's programmes at KTH with two years spent at KTH, the joint master's programmes in Molecular Techniques in Life Science and in Biostatistics and Data Science, and the one-year master's programme in Architectural Lighting Design (NOT joint Erasmus+/EIT programmes or Computer Simulations for Science and Engineering - see the KTH Joint Programme Scholarship instead)"]$j$, eligible_countries = $j$["Students liable for tuition fees in Sweden (non-EU/EEA/Swiss citizens without an exempting residence permit)"]$j$, min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$The KTH Scholarship covers the full tuition fee of a one- or two-year master's programme at KTH Royal Institute of Technology - for the first and the second year, provided the study results during the first year are satisfactory. It does not include living costs. The selection focuses on academic excellence and drive to contribute to sustainable development, and it is genuinely selective: in 2026, 9% of the scholarship applicants admitted to a programme were nominated for the KTH Scholarship (65 out of 718). The single most important eligibility rule is the priority rule - you must be a fee-paying student who has applied for a master's programme at KTH as your first priority at universityadmissions.se and paid the application fee; you cannot apply for or be awarded the scholarship for programmes listed as your second, third or fourth priority. Eligible programmes are all master's programmes with two years spent at KTH, the joint master's programmes in Molecular Techniques in Life Science and Biostatistics and Data Science (the Stockholm Trio programmes), and the one-year master's programme in Architectural Lighting Design; joint Erasmus+ and EIT programmes and the joint programme Computer Simulations for Science and Engineering are excluded (some of those feed the separate KTH Joint Programme Scholarship, and KTH also runs a One-Year Scholarship for current students and an India-specific scholarship). The procedure is two-step: first the programme application at universityadmissions.se (deadline 15 January 2027 in the current round, documents by 1 February), then the scholarship application form on the KTH Scholarship page - no additional documents are needed for the scholarship, as KTH evaluates the documents already submitted for admission.$desc$, requirements = $req$Fee-paying (non-EU/EEA/Swiss without an exempting permit) applicants who fulfil the admission requirements of their chosen programme are eligible only if KTH is their first priority on universityadmissions.se and the application fee is paid; second-, third- or fourth-priority programmes cannot carry the scholarship. After admission assessment, scholarship candidates are assessed on: the applicant's grades (GPA or equivalent); the ranking of the university that awarded the bachelor's degree; extracurricular research experience or publications, relevant work and teaching experience, competition awards and extracurricular activities; and the applicant's stated motivation for contributing to the sustainable development goals with a KTH master's degree. Continuation into the second year requires satisfactory first-year study results. The scholarship covers tuition only - Stockholm living costs are entirely the student's. Grades are assessed comparatively (no published numeric cutoff), and no scholarship-level IELTS figure exists (English requirements belong to programme admission), so min_gpa/min_ielts are not recorded.$req$, website_url = 'https://www.kth.se/en/studies/master/admissions/scholarships/kth-scholarship-1.72827', source_url = 'https://www.kth.se/en/studies/master/admissions/scholarships/kth-scholarship-1.72827', application_url = 'https://www.universityadmissions.se', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'upcoming', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 111) from KTH's official KTH Scholarship page and scholarship-opportunities overview fetched the same day (full tuition fee of a one- or two-year master's covered for years one and two conditional on satisfactory first-year results; no living costs; 9% nomination rate in 2026 - 65 of 718 admitted applicants; strict first-priority rule at universityadmissions.se with the application fee paid; eligible programmes = two-year-at-KTH master's plus the Molecular Techniques in Life Science and Biostatistics and Data Science joint programmes and the one-year Architectural Lighting Design, excluding Erasmus+/EIT joint programmes and Computer Simulations for Science and Engineering, which route to the KTH Joint Programme Scholarship; two-step application with the scholarship form on the KTH page and admission documents due 1 February; four-part selection criteria including sustainable-development motivation; sibling schemes KTH One-Year and KTH India noted on the overview). The previously stored URL (kth.se/en/studies/master/scholarships/...) returns 404; the live page sits under /admissions/. Award stored as NULL (SEK, 'year', 'variable'): a 100% waiver whose krona value follows the programme fee, which the fetched page does not price. deadline_date 2027-01-15 is the binding first-step deadline of Sweden's first admission round (programme application at universityadmissions.se; the 15 January / 1 February 2027 round dates were read the same day on the University of Gothenburg's scholarship page for the same national round, and the KTH page itself cites the 1 February document deadline); status 'upcoming' because on the verification date the scholarship form's own window was not shown as open even though programme applications already are - both steps are spelled out in the deadline text. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL. university_scholarships row 83 synced; source 2557 repointed from the bare kth.se domain to the live official page. Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with no terms read.$note$, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = 'SEK', award_period = 'year', award_basis = 'variable', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'Full tuition fee covered for a one- or two-year master''s programme (second year conditional on satisfactory first-year results); living costs not included', tuition_coverage = 'The scholarship covers the tuition fee at KTH in full for the programme duration stated (one or two years); the fee amount itself varies by programme and is not part of this award''s terms.', english_requirements = 'No scholarship-level IELTS figure; English proficiency is assessed under the master''s programme admission requirements.', required_documents = $j$["Master's programme application at universityadmissions.se with KTH as FIRST priority and the application fee paid (by 15 January 2027; supporting documents by 1 February 2027)", "KTH Scholarship application form on the KTH Scholarship page (no additional documents - KTH uses the admission documents)", "In the scholarship application: account of how you intend to contribute to sustainable development with a KTH master's degree"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"round": "Autumn 2027 entry (first admission round)", "programme_deadline": "2027-01-15", "documents_by": "2027-02-01", "status": "upcoming"}, {"pattern": "Annual, inside Sweden's first (international) admission round: programme application mid-October to 15 January, documents by 1 February, scholarship application on the KTH page in the same round; selection runs in parallel with admissions"}]$json$ WHERE id = 325;

-- ═══ 421 Chalmers Master's Scholarships ═══
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'Chalmers Master''s Scholarships for Fee-Paying Students (Avancez, IPOET, Adlerbert, US Friends)', provider = 'Chalmers University of Technology', coverage_type = 'Tuition Waiver', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'Separate scholarship application in the Chalmers portal once you have applied to a master''s programme at universityadmissions.se (you need your 8-digit application number): for the 2027 admission round the scholarship application opens in late November 2026 and the scholarship deadline aligns with the programme application deadline in mid-January 2027 (15 January) - NOT with the later supporting-documents deadline. Offers are sent between March and the beginning of May.', deadline_date = '2027-01-15', deadline_type = 'fixed', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Master's"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["Master's programmes at Chalmers University of Technology (prospective students only - not open to current students; some schemes are limited by citizenship or by education area)"]$j$, eligible_countries = $j$["Students liable for tuition fees in Sweden (non-EU/EEA/Swiss citizens without an exempting residence permit); the US Friends of Chalmers Scholarship is for US citizens and the Adlerbert Study Scholarships are tied to a list of eligible countries"]$j$, min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$Chalmers administers its master's scholarships for fee-paying students through one portal and one set of Scholarship Regulations, and this record covers that Chalmers-administered family: the Avancez Scholarships, the IPOET Scholarships (educational-cooperation scholarships funded via the Swedish government/UHR), the Adlerbert Study Scholarships and the US Friends of Chalmers Scholarship. The two flagship schemes work as follows: Avancez and IPOET are awarded in the form of a 75% reduction of the tuition fee (Avancez quotas are allocated to Chalmers' education areas based on the previous year's on-time first-priority applications), and particularly excellent students who complete the first year at the conventional pace (60 credits) with a high weighted average (CGPA) may be granted a further reduction to the 85% level during the second year - decided yearly, notified in the third semester and applied as a 95% reduction on the fourth-semester bill. All Chalmers-administered scholarships are tuition-fee reductions, not cash: they are awarded on relative merit (with an ambition for a good spread of bachelor's universities and countries), financial status plays no part in the nomination (external complementary funding does not hurt), and they must be earned to be kept - an awardee must pass at least 30 credits in the first three study periods (registered by 15 May) to retain the scholarship for the following academic year, the reduction covers at most 120 credits of the named master's programme, deferment voids the offer, and a programme transfer triggers reassessment. The application is a genuinely separate step: first apply to the programme(s) at universityadmissions.se (rank a Chalmers programme as priority 1 to maximise scholarship chances), then apply in the Chalmers scholarship portal with the 8-digit application number; for 2027 admission the scholarship window runs from late November 2026 to the programme deadline in mid-January 2027, offers go out between March and early May, and only applicants who end up fulfilling the programme eligibility requirements are finally considered.$desc$, requirements = $req$Prospective fee-paying master's students only (current Chalmers students cannot apply; applications must precede the first academic year). Sequence matters: submit the programme application at universityadmissions.se first - the 8-digit application number is required for the scholarship portal, where one form can cover multiple Chalmers-administered scholarships if their requirements are met; the scholarship deadline aligns with the programme application deadline (mid-January), and the application is only processed once the programme application is complete (documents uploaded by the documentation deadline and the application fee paid) - missing either disqualifies it. Ranking a Chalmers programme as priority 1 is crucial to the assessment. Awards rest on relative merit value plus the regulations' distribution ambition (bachelor's institutions/countries); an applicant's financial status is not considered. Retention requires at least 30 passed credits in the first three study periods as registered by 15 May; the 85% second-year uplift for Avancez/IPOET additionally requires 60 credits at conventional pace with a high CGPA. Changing to fee-exempt status ends the waiver part; deferment voids the offer. No numeric GPA cutoff (relative merit) or scholarship-level IELTS figure is published, so min_gpa/min_ielts are not recorded. Note: Chalmers' page states it is not yet updated with the 2027-round scheme details - the per-scheme conditions recorded here are those of the current official page and the 2024 Scholarship Regulations it links.$req$, website_url = 'https://www.chalmers.se/en/education/application-and-admission/scholarships-for-fee-paying-students/', source_url = 'https://www.chalmers.se/en/education/application-and-admission/scholarships-for-fee-paying-students/', application_url = 'https://scholarship.portal.chalmers.se/', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'upcoming', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 9, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 111) from Chalmers' official 'Scholarships for fee-paying students' page, its 'How to apply' subpage and the linked Scholarship Regulations (version 2024), all fetched the same day (Chalmers-administered master's scholarships: Avancez, IPOET, Adlerbert Study Scholarships, US Friends of Chalmers; separate portal application after the universityadmissions.se programme application using the 8-digit application number; 2027-round window late November 2026 to mid-January 2027 with the scholarship deadline aligning to the programme deadline, offers March to early May; prospective students only; offers valid for two years under the Regulations; Avancez/IPOET at a 75% tuition reduction with a possible uplift to the 85% level in year two for 60-credit high-CGPA performance applied as 95% off the fourth semester; Avancez allocated across education areas by first-priority application counts; retention requires at least 30 passed credits in the first three study periods by 15 May; maximum 120 credits; deferment voids; relative-merit awarding with distribution ambition; financial status disregarded; priority-1 ranking guidance). Reliability 9 rather than 10: the fetched Chalmers page itself states it is 'not yet updated with the information regarding Chalmers scholarships offered in 2027 admission round', and while Avancez/IPOET values come from the official Regulations, the individual 2027 terms of the Adlerbert and US Friends schemes were named and framed but not individually re-priced in this pass - no percentages are stated for those two here. Award stored as NULL (SEK, 'year', 'variable'): percentage reductions whose krona value follows the programme fee. Title broadened from the stored 'Chalmers Avancez & IPOET Scholarships' to the full Chalmers-administered family exactly as the official page presents it (one application, several named schemes). The stored URL returns 404; the page moved under /application-and-admission/. deadline_date 2027-01-15 = the programme application deadline the scholarship deadline 'aligns with' in Sweden's first round, with status 'upcoming' because the scholarship portal opens only in late November 2026. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL. university_scholarships row 107 synced; source 2500 repointed from the bare chalmers.se domain to the live official page. Previous record held the schemes at reliability 4 with no terms read. Related externally administered routes named on the page (SI scholarships; COLFUTURO/FIDERH/FUNED; country funds) are outside this record.$note$, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = 'SEK', award_period = 'year', award_basis = 'variable', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'Tuition-fee reductions via one portal application: Avancez and IPOET cut the tuition fee by 75% (rising to the 85% level in year two for students completing 60 credits with a high CGPA); the Adlerbert Study Scholarships and the US Friends of Chalmers Scholarship are the further Chalmers-administered schemes in the same application. Retention requires at least 30 passed credits in the first three study periods.', tuition_coverage = 'Avancez/IPOET: 75% of the tuition fee waived, potentially 85%-level in year two; all Chalmers-administered scholarships are fee reductions (max 120 credits of the named programme), never living-cost support - the remaining fee share must be paid by the deadline.', english_requirements = 'No scholarship-level IELTS figure; English requirements follow each master''s programme''s admission rules.', required_documents = $j$["Programme application at universityadmissions.se first (rank a Chalmers programme as priority 1) - the resulting 8-digit application number is required for the scholarship portal", "Scholarship application in the Chalmers scholarship portal during the scholarship window (same e-mail address as the universityadmissions.se account; editable until the deadline)", "Complete programme application behind it: application fee paid and all eligibility documents uploaded by the documentation deadline, otherwise the scholarship application is not considered"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"round": "2027 admission", "scholarship_window": "late November 2026 - 2027-01-15", "offers": "2027-03 to 2027-05", "status": "upcoming"}, {"pattern": "Annual: programme application at universityadmissions.se in the autumn round, then the scholarship portal from late November until the mid-January programme deadline; offers between March and early May; retention and uplift assessed on credits/CGPA during the degree"}]$json$ WHERE id = 421;

-- ═══ 422 RETIRE (duplicate of 673) ═══
UPDATE scholarships SET is_active = false, application_status = 'closed', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = NULL, tuition_coverage = NULL, english_requirements = NULL, required_documents = NULL, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = NULL, notes = $note$Retired on 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 111) as a duplicate. Stockholm University's official scholarships page (fetched 2026-10-27; the URL stored on this row is superseded) lists exactly one Stockholm University tuition instrument for ordinary master's applicants - the Stockholm University Scholarship Scheme, which covers the whole tuition fee for a Master's programme (students cover living costs), for non-EU/EEA/Swiss citizens admitted in the first (international) admission round, with the application form emailed to eligible students when selection results are published and results by the end of April. That scheme is already catalogued accurately as record 673 ('Stockholm University Scholarship Scheme', reliability 9); this record's generic title, 'Stockholm University Tuition Fee Waiver', names the same whole-fee waiver and would duplicate it, so the reliability-4 copy is retired rather than rewritten. (The other instruments on the same page - Swedish Institute scholarships, the Stockholm Trio Scholarship for the two joint programmes and the arbitration-law scholarships for ICAL - are separate schemes that this row never identified; they remain future-additions candidates.) Kept for audit only; not a discoverable scholarship. university_scholarships row 628 withdrawn; source 2623 (previously the bare su.se domain) repointed to the official scholarships page used for this determination.$note$, last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 422;

-- ═══ 423 RETIRE (duplicate of 739) ═══
UPDATE scholarships SET is_active = false, application_status = 'closed', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = NULL, tuition_coverage = NULL, english_requirements = NULL, required_documents = NULL, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = NULL, notes = $note$Retired on 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 111) as a duplicate. This record's title, 'Gothenburg Axel Adler Scholarship', is the Axel Adler Scholarship of the University of Gothenburg - the tuition fee waiver for first-choice applicants to international campus-based bachelor's and master's programmes (funded by the Adlerbertska foundations and the Swedish Council for Higher Education), whose current official page (fetched 2026-10-27, with the live 2027-round calendar: study application by 15 January 2027, documents/fee by 1 February 2027, scholarship invitation around 10 February 2027, results 12/15 April 2027) is the very page catalogued as record 739 ('Axel Adler Scholarship (University of Gothenburg)', reliability 9). The stored record here even had the level scope wrong (Master's only, while the scheme covers eligible bachelor's programmes too, as 739 records). Rewriting it would produce a second, weaker copy of 739, so the reliability-4 duplicate is retired. The smaller Axel Adler Scholarship for Sustainability variant (2-12 students in sustainability-focused master's programmes, same application) was never this row's identity and remains a future-additions candidate. Kept for audit only; not a discoverable scholarship. university_scholarships row 629 withdrawn; source 2533 (previously the bare gu.se domain) repointed to the official Axel Adler Scholarship page used for this determination.$note$, last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 423;

